{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Samsen879/ciecopilot-home/pulls/1533","id":4036103319,"node_id":"PR_kwDOO5D6p87wkgyX","html_url":"https://github.com/Samsen879/ciecopilot-home/pull/1533","diff_url":"https://github.com/Samsen879/ciecopilot-home/pull/1533.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/Samsen879/ciecopilot-home/pull/1533.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Samsen879/ciecopilot-home/issues/1533","number":1533,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"security: enforce auth and rate limits on direct RAG routes","user":{"login":"Samsen879","id":172257175,"node_id":"U_kgDOCkRvlw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/172257175?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879","html_url":"https://github.com/Samsen879","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Samsen879/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Root cause\n\n`api/rag/ask.js` and `api/rag/search.js` were callable as file-based/serverless handlers without inheriting `api/index.js` gateway controls. They normalized input and called `executeAskAI` directly, so direct entrypoints bypassed JWT authentication and `rag_ai_default_v1` rate limiting.\n\n## Direct exposure analysis\n\n- `api/rag/ask.js`: direct handler had method validation, normalization, `executeAskAI`, and RAG telemetry only; no auth or rate-limit guard.\n- `api/rag/search.js`: same direct-entry exposure and the same `executeAskAI` pipeline.\n- Repository callers found: the central gateway loads both handlers through `api/_runtime/handler-loader.js`; focused handler tests import them directly. No `api/rag/chat.js` was changed or added.\n\n## Deployment topology analysis\n\nThe repository has a central Node gateway (`api/index.js`) plus file-based `api/**` handlers. The registry maps `/api/rag/ask` and `/api/rag/search` to the two direct files. No deployment manifest in the repository was changed; direct handler exposure is therefore treated as a possible file-based/serverless deployment surface and is now fail-closed at the handler boundary.\n\n## Affected handlers and gateway contract\n\nAffected handlers are `/api/rag/ask` (`rag-ask`) and `/api/rag/search` (`rag-search`). Both canonical registry entries specify `jwt_required`, `authMode: authenticated`, and `rateLimitPolicyId: rag_ai_default_v1`. The effective policy is 10 authenticated-user requests/minute and 5 IP requests/minute, with a 60-second window and matching burst limits.\n\nBefore this change, the gateway order was method check → auth → rate limit → handler, while direct calls performed only method check. The gateway now and direct handlers now use one shared enforcement path in that same auth-before-rate-limit order.\n\n## Shared guard and double-enforcement prevention\n\n`api/lib/security/route-security-guard.js` is the single enforcement path. It calls the existing `requireAuth`, `applyRateLimitGuard`, canonical security failure helpers, degraded-rate-limit logging, and the existing 429 envelope with `Retry-After`. Direct handlers resolve their own route object from the route registry; they do not copy limits or policy objects. Missing, malformed, or mismatched direct route security contracts fail closed.\n\nThe guard stores auth and rate-limit promises in module-private request-object `WeakMap` state keyed by the canonical route object. Therefore gateway → handler invocation, repeated guard calls, and concurrent reuse of the same request do not repeat downstream auth lookup or consume a rate-limit token twice. No request header, query, body, cookie, or external marker is trusted as a completion signal.\n\n## Auth and rate-limit behavior before/after\n\n- Missing, malformed, invalid, expired, or configuration-failed auth now returns the canonical 401/500 security envelope before `executeAskAI`; auth rejection does not consume rate limit or record RAG model telemetry.\n- Auth success sets and preserves `req.auth_context`, `req.auth_user_id`, and `req.auth_user`; client-provided `user_id` values do not override verified identity.\n- Allowed authenticated calls preserve existing input normalization, response shapes, RAG pipeline behavior, and telemetry behavior.\n- Denied calls return 429 with `Retry-After >= 1`, do not call `executeAskAI`, and do not record model-call telemetry.\n- Degraded-but-allowed rate limiting retains existing logging/degrade semantics.\n\n## Tests and results\n\nPassed locally with mocked provider/retrieval boundaries and no remote Supabase:\n\n- Direct route security: 16 tests.\n- Shared route-security guard: 7 tests.\n- Registry policy matrix, collision, and auth-context tests: included in a 45-test focused security/telemetry/auth run; all passed.\n- Gateway security baseline/depth, shared rate limit, and API route integration: 22 tests; all passed.\n- RAG ask/search characterization: 56 tests; all passed.\n- Telemetry/auth middleware tests: 9 tests; all passed.\n- ESLint on all changed JavaScript: passed.\n- Workflow YAML parse: passed.\n- `git diff --check`: passed.\n- `npm run workflow:codex-preflight -- --json`: passed with the expected dirty-worktree warning before commit; final clean-state preflight is included in handoff.\n\nThe first sandbox attempt at listener-based tests failed with `listen EPERM`; the same tests were rerun in the approved controlled environment and passed. No real embedding, retrieval, LLM, or provider call was made.\n\n## GitHub Actions checks\n\nChanged paths are under `api/**`, which already triggers API Route Integration Gate, Security Depth Gate, Security Baseline Gate, Shared Rate Limit Gate, and the repository-wide Lint Gate. No workflow path-filter change was necessary. CI remains GitHub-hosted and does not use repository secrets or self-hosted execution for this change.\n\n## Review thread status\n\nNew PR; no review threads yet.\n\n## Remaining limitations\n\nThis change hardens the repository's direct handler trust boundary. Deployment-specific routing outside this repository is not modified or independently verified. The change intentionally does not address the separately excluded RLS, privilege-escalation, cross-user view, recommendation, or RAG-log findings, and does not change retrieval, embedding, provider, prompt, ranking, response contracts, schema, or product behavior.\n\nNo remote Supabase was connected to or modified.\n","created_at":"2026-07-11T16:25:40Z","updated_at":"2026-07-12T06:52:01Z","closed_at":"2026-07-12T06:52:01Z","merged_at":"2026-07-12T06:52:01Z","merge_commit_sha":"1ce88e98c4db00687e3128fdc7077b4d49799052","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Samsen879/ciecopilot-home/pulls/1533/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Samsen879/ciecopilot-home/pulls/1533/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Samsen879/ciecopilot-home/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Samsen879/ciecopilot-home/issues/1533/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Samsen879/ciecopilot-home/statuses/e39ef25bd07550c493a78a3a20ee33068553246a","head":{"label":"Samsen879:codex/direct-rag-route-security","ref":"codex/direct-rag-route-security","sha":"e39ef25bd07550c493a78a3a20ee33068553246a","user":{"login":"Samsen879","id":172257175,"node_id":"U_kgDOC